# Cost-optimized budget strategy

The team with the lowest cost wins extra marks. Here is a realistic strategy to come in at approximately €75 – saving over 80% of the €400 budget.

| **Work Package** | **Make or Buy** | **Budget** | **Target** | **Cost-saving tip** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Control Board** | HW buy / SW develop | < 100 € | **~15 €** | Arduino Nano clone (~5€) + buttons + LM2596 buck module |
| **Driver Electronics** | Buy or develop | < 100 € | **~5 €** | IR2104 gate driver IC (~2€) + bootstrap caps + resistors |
| **Power Electronics** | Develop | < 100 € | **~10 €** | IRFZ44N MOSFET (~1€) + shunt resistor + flyback diode + heatsink |
| **DC Motor** | Buy | < 100 € | **~30 €** | Search Amazon.de / eBay.de for MY1016 or similar 24V 250W |
| **Power Supply** | Given / option buy | < 200 € | **0 €** | Use lab power supply (free!) – battery only if prof requires it |
| **Connectors ****&**** cables** | Buy | (included) | **~15 €** | Screw terminals, XT60, cables, wooden board, standoffs |
| **TOTAL** |  | **400 €** | **~75 €** | **Savings of ~325€ vs budget – this impresses the professor!** |

