# Week-by-week action checklist

## Week 1: 26.03 – 01.04 (Block diagram week)

- Draw complete system block diagram with all 5 work packages

- Define every interface: signal type, voltage level, current

- Decide on MCU platform (Arduino Nano recommended for cost)

- Research motor options on Amazon.de / eBay.de (24V, 250W, brushed)

- Specify wooden board dimensions (suggested: 40×30 cm)

- Assign work packages to team members

## Week 2: 02.04 – 08.04 (Present block diagram + prep for Pres. 1)

- Submit block diagram to professor on 02.04

- Select MCU and voltage regulator – finalize Control Board design

- Define power supply requirements (voltage, current capacity)

- Begin schematic for Control Board in KiCad

- Prepare presentation slides for 2 work packages

## Week 3: 09.04 – 15.04 (Holiday week – use for prep!)

- Finalize Control Board + Power Supply schematics

- Rehearse Presentation 1 (16.04)

- Begin researching gate driver ICs for Driver Electronics

- Order motor if a good option is found (delivery ≤ 1 week)

## Week 4: 16.04 – 22.04 (Presentation 1 + Driver Electronics)

- Deliver Presentation 1 on 16.04 (Control Board + Power Supply)

- Design Driver Electronics circuit (gate driver + bootstrap)

- Select and order DC motor if not already done

- Begin software development: PWM generation, button handling

## Week 5: 23.04 – 29.04 (Prep for Presentation 2)

- Finalize Driver Electronics schematic

- Document motor specifications from datasheet

- Prepare Presentation 2 slides (Driver Electronics + DC Motor)

- Continue software: ADC for current sensing, overcurrent logic

## Week 6: 30.04 – 06.05 (Presentation 2 + Power Electronics)

- Deliver Presentation 2 on 30.04 (Driver Electronics + DC Motor)

- Design Power Electronics circuit (MOSFET + current sensor + flyback diode)

- Thermal calculations for MOSFET (heatsink sizing)

- Specify all connection materials (connectors, cables, terminals)

- Prepare Presentation 3 slides

## Week 7: 07.05 – 20.05 (Presentation 3 + BOM finalization)

- Deliver Presentation 3 on 07.05 (Power Electronics + connections)

- All 5 work packages now presented – integrate feedback

- Compile complete BOM with prices and delivery sources

- Verify all delivery times ≤ 1 week

- Submit final BOM by 21.05

- Place all remaining orders immediately after BOM approval

## Weeks 8–9: 21.05 – 03.06 (PCB + Software + Assembly)

- Complete PCB layout in KiCad by 28.05

- Complete software with all mandatory features by 28.05

- Order PCBs (or build on perfboard for faster turnaround)

- Begin hardware assembly on wooden board

- Test individual subsystems before integration

- Integration testing: MCU → Driver → MOSFET → Motor

- Prepare draft report by 04.06

## Weeks 10–12: 04.06 – 25.06 (Report + Final Presentation)

- Submit draft report on 04.06 – incorporate professor feedback

- Submit final report on 11.06

- Debug and polish the prototype

- Prepare final presentation slides

- Rehearse live demo: motor on/off, speed up/down, overcurrent trip

- Final Presentation on 25.06 at 11:30 – 11:50

*Remember: The professor values cost efficiency, documentation quality, and a working demo. Aim for ~€75 total spend, clean schematics, and a reliable prototype that doesn’t fail during the live demo.*